      "side": 1,
      "message": "Does every HttpContent end on an SSE line boundary? Http3FrameCodec emits partial DATA frames as QUIC packets arrive (~1200 bytes), so a larger notification gets split into two bogus fields, and a split right after \"data:\" makes SseUtils.parseChunks call charAt past the end, which closes the stream. Could the handler buffer the incomplete trailing line between chunks (and guard that charAt)?\n\nNone of the HTTP/3 SSE tests sends an event big enough to be split across QUIC packets like that. Could we add a test that streams one event over 2 KB over HTTP/3 and checks the data field arrives intact? I suspect it would currently arrive as two broken fields, because processChunks parses each chunk as whole lines.",
      "revId": "10c33c40897c677029b8d7cf1d231c0436fce5d6",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
